hypotheses.statement:
Let $k\ge3$ and $2\le a\le k$ be integers, and let $G$ be a finite simple graph such that $$|V(G)|=ka+1,\qquad \alpha(G)\le a,\qquad C_{k+1}\not\subseteq G.$$ Suppose also that $$|N_G[I]|\ge k|I|+1
 \quad\text{for every nonempty independent set }I\subseteq V(G).$$ Then its maximum clique size $t$ satisfies $$\label{clq:bound-equation}
 \max\{3,\lfloor k/2\rfloor\}\le t\le k.$$

For $i\in X$, put $$b_0=k+1-n_X+|\{j\in X:0\in M_{ij}\}|.$$ Assume $b_0>0$, and define $$u_0=1+\mathbf 1_{\{b_0\ge t\}}.$$ For $r=1,2$, recursively set $$\begin{aligned}
 A_r(i)&=\{j\in X:\{1,\ldots,r\}\subseteq M_{ij}\},
 &T_r&=|A_r(i)|,\label{finite:excluded-neighbors}\\
 b_r&=\max\{b_{r-1},\,ku_{r-1}+1-n_X+T_r\},\label{finite:ball-size}\\
 \widehat u_r&=\max\bigl\{u_{r-1},
       1+\mathbf 1_{\{b_r>t\}}
        +\mathbf 1_{\{b_r>\max(k,2t)\}}\bigr\}.
       \label{finite:ordinary-weight}
\end{aligned}$$ Set $u_r=\widehat u_r$, except that $u_r=2$ when $$\label{finite:exception-condition}
 \widehat u_r=1,\qquad b_{r-1}=b_r=t,\qquad
 k+1-n_X+T_r\ge t.$$ Then, for $r=0,1,2$, $$|B_r(i;X)|\ge b_r,\qquad \alpha(B_r(i;X))\ge u_r.$$

Let a family of these options have distinct base vertices. For options based at $i,j$ with radius labels $r,s$, require $$\label{finite:compatibility}
 \begin{cases}
 0\in M_{ij},&r=s=-1,\\
 \{1,\ldots,r+s+2\}\subseteq M_{ij},&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}$$ If every pair satisfies this condition, the sum of the option weights is at most $k$.

